-- Second, more aggressive dropdown-conversion pass on marketplace
-- attribute_schema content, per direct product-owner example (Cars: Model
-- became a Brand-dependent select, Year/Seats/Engine Size/Horsepower became
-- selects instead of free number/stepper inputs). Extends the same treatment
-- to 24 subcategories: dependent Model selects wherever a curatable
-- brand roster exists (motorcycles/buses/trucks, phones/tablets/watches),
-- and bucketing continuous specs into their real-world standard values
-- (screen sizes, engine displacement/capacity, generator KVA, aquarium
-- litres, feed-bag kg, livestock/bird breed lists) where precision doesn't
-- matter as much as picking a common value. Only touches subcategories that
-- actually changed; everything else keeps its content from
-- 20270151000000/20270153000000 unchanged. Same dual-shape convention --
-- see docs/adr/ADR-PR-marketplace-attribute-schema-enrichment.md.
--
-- Additive-only: UPDATEs the JSONB column on existing rows, no DDL.
-- Idempotent: unconditional UPDATE keyed by (market_id, slug).

